  "modified": "2026-09-04T14:04:18Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: Heap buffer overflow in to_char(timestamptz).\n     DCH_to_char() copied the timezone abbreviation into a workspace\n     budgeted at DCH_MAX_ITEM_SIZ bytes per format character with an\n     unchecked strcpy(), and any client can select a longer POSIX\n     abbreviation via SET TIME ZONE (CVSS 8.8, arbitrary code execution\n     as the database OS user).\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-14669.patch: reject POSIX timezone\n       abbreviations longer than n->key->len * DCH_MAX_ITEM_SIZ in the\n       TZ/tz items of DCH_to_char() with an error, instead of strcpy()ing\n       them past the palloc'd buffer (upstream 3d724bf4fd, backpatched to\n       REL_14_STABLE as the formatting.c hunk of 5fb3c638 and shipped in\n       14.24; applies verbatim).\n     - CVE-2026-14669",
